  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>At 42 Nouveau Port in Cavalaire-sur-Mer, Le Bateau Ivre is a brasserie with a sunny terrace facing the sea, perfect for a morning coffee or a meal while watching the boats in the harbour. The menu mixes fresh seafood (whole sea bass, smoked salmon, prawns, baby squid with parsley) with Italian and Mediterranean specialities (gnocchi, penne, risotto).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>This is a spot the Coco Explore team knows personally, having had coffee on the terrace there several times: the owner and staff are very friendly and love dogs, to the point of having already brought out a water bowl or a small biscuit for a passing dog without being asked. Open every day from 8am to 10:30pm according to the official website. The phone number listed comes from the restaurant's official website, but could not be cross-checked by a second independent source — worth confirming if needed before booking.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the terrace is in full sun for much of the day — think about a shady spot or water for your dog if you stop by in the middle of the day in summer.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Cavalaire harbour and its promenade are great for a walk before or after the meal, and the <a href="/en/fiche-dogwash-port-cavalaire">dog wash at the harbour</a> is just a few minutes' walk away for a rinse after the beach.</p>
    </div>

